  "text": "The city breathes in neon light,\nWhere shadows stretch and footsteps bite\nThe pavement’s cold, unyielding stone,\nAlone beneath the streetlamp’s zone.\n\nLike phantoms drift the passing crowd,\nWith eyes cast down, no words are loud,\nBuried deep in private thought,\nWhere silent, solitary lives are caught.\n\nAmidst the sea of concrete tide,\nWith nowhere left for him to hide,\nA hollow ache, a vast divide,\nIn solitude, he stands inside.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
